:

- **`sable-vellum`** (C-1b5c9f63): wires a 3-way classification task (`card_sortis`) into an installed micro lm-eval harness (`vellum_eval`), with a generic HTTP dataset driver; gold indices come from the declared `choices` order, so a wrong order/gold mapping collapses accuracy to ~0.3, far outside the graded 0.60–0.95 window (true accuracy 0.882). Verifier re-runs the driver on 3 hidden corpora served over loopback HTTP and recomputes every metric independently.
- **`fume-latch`** (C-e797cde5): per-line defect repair against an HTTP fix desk with a budget equal to the work-order size; any extra fix request flips the session to `budget-exceeded` and fails the run. Verifier re-runs the delivered client on 3 fresh hidden sessions (shuffled order, double-space byte-exact repair, redundant no-op entry, no trailing newline) and independently checks plate bytes, receipt sha256, and session status.

Debug iterations used: 2 fixes for sable-vellum (inverted `if !` verifier logic), 2 for fume-latch (off-by-one line numbers in hidden work orders + same verifier logic bug) — within the 3-attempt budget.

